{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791540997,"nonce":"aGbYe5TLrL2ZYPqJpCBy/OoAHqc=","title":"Cranelift reserves one word for fixed-size stack arrays","message":"Pinned Cranelift Reflect.callMethod with eight arguments fails or corrupts its closure pointer; LLVM passes the same source. Reproducer: DynamicFunctionCasts.hx and /tmp/ReflectManyProbe.hx. CLIF dumps /tmp/rayzor-packed-clif-v7.log and /tmp/reflect-many-main-v7.log show explicit_slot 8 followed by pointer stores at offsets 0 through 56. Runtime tracing shows a live closure overwritten with a TYPE_INT box, followed by SIGBUS at pc=3.\n\ninstruction_lowering.rs type_size defaults IrType::Array to eight bytes. Compute element size times count recursively and reject size overflow. DynamicFunctionCasts covers direct and reflected eight-argument adapters, with numeric conversions and a preserved typed argument array. Parent Dynamic call ABI issue: 3739d2e1f64d7940ff11b43bb0e1fe1131571232c80243277122c769a35bfa94. Full conformance and regression validation pending.","files":null}]}